course: dictionary
lesson: 4871
title: Icy: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word icy can mean covered with ice, extremely cold, or unfriendly. The words around it tell you which meaning to use.
explain: «The icy playground was slippery, so we walked slowly.» The clue is slippery, so icy means covered with ice. Now try a different sentence: «The icy wind made our cheeks sting.» The clue is sting, so icy here means extremely cold.
explain: «She gave him an icy stare and did not smile.» The clue is did not smile, so icy means very unfriendly. Always check the clues, then put your meaning into the sentence to see if it fits.
fact: Icy means covered with ice, as in «an icy road».
fact: Icy also means extremely cold, as in «an icy wind».
fact: An icy look or voice is very unfriendly, as in «an icy stare».
fact: Icy roads and pavements are slippery, so walk slowly and wear good shoes.
fact: Never walk on an icy pond or lake, because the ice may break.
exercise: «Grit or sand sprinkled on an icy path gives shoes more grip.» What does icy mean in this sentence? | Very unfriendly | Very happy | Covered in mud | *Covered with ice
exercise: «She gave him an icy stare and turned away.» What does icy mean here? | Sparkling in the sun | Extremely cold weather | Covered with ice | *Very unfriendly
exercise: «The icy wind made our cheeks sting.» Which word in this sentence means extremely cold? | sting | cheeks | wind | *icy
test: «Walk slowly on the icy pavements.» What does icy mean here? | *Covered with ice | Covered in mud | Very happy | Very unfriendly
test: Why must you never walk on an icy pond? | It is full of fish | It is too sunny to walk on | It is too deep to swim in | *The ice may break under you
exam: Which sentence uses icy to mean very unfriendly? | «The icy road was closed for the day.» | *«Her icy voice told me to go away.» | «The icy patch was marked with a sign.» | «An icy wind blew across the hill.»
